# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS for the craft and art ladders (v25 prep, Library, 10-23).
# Draft for the Library to pour into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib on Friday. Nothing reads this yet.
# Thirteen moments a shape (practice x2, contest x2, mentor, rival, setback, plateau, cost, chance, round, reaction,
# arrive), worded once with the field's slots, in the balance layout: five single ways and one full cross cycle.
# Cycle 1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W. Cycle 2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W. Craft starts on cycle 1, art on cycle 2 (13 each).
# Craft fields: building that lasts, cooking, making video games. Art fields: an instrument, dance, a band, and the
# packs' art and stage fields. Craft rungs: learner, journeyman, trusted hand, master, a name in the craft.
# Art rungs: trying, showing, a following, recognised, a body of work.

# ================================================================ CRAFT

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- craft practice, low rungs (cycle 1)

== the long evening at {aim.place}
tier: life event
shape: craft
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: work, interests
horizon: week
roles: mentor, friend, rival
earth: an ordinary evening of {aim.doing} at {aim.place}, the slow part that adds up
tribal: an evening of {aim.doing} by the fire, the slow part the elders say adds up
magic: an evening of {aim.doing} in the tower's workrooms, the slow part the masters say adds up
scene: {N} has been {aim.doing} at {aim.place} for three hours, and the same small part still will not come right. Across the room {aim.person} looks over once, says nothing, and goes back to their own work.
scene tribal: By the fire {N} goes over the same small part of the work again and again. An elder watches from the dark and says nothing, which is a kind of praise.
scene magic: In the tower's workrooms {N} repeats the same small part of the work until the lamps burn low. A master passes the door and nods once.
- W | do the part again, exactly as you were shown, until it is right | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- U | take the part apart to see why it keeps going wrong | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson the mistake shows the way | chance: 72
- B | stay later than everyone else, so the people who matter notice | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 65
- R | leave it, and make something quick and wild just for fun | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: ease | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 78
- G | put the tools down and go home in time for supper | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
- W>U | write down every step in a notebook kept for the purpose | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 76
- U>B | ask {aim.person} for the trick behind it, and offer an hour's help in return | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 68
- B>R | race {friend} to finish first, and the slower one tidies up | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: means ties+.02 | chance: 70
- R>G | open the door, put music on and work at whatever pace comes | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: lesson a light hand works better | chance: 80
- G>W | help the youngest one at the next bench with theirs first | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: ease | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
works: The small part comes right at last, and {N} does it twice more to be sure it was not luck.
works: Nothing grand happens tonight, but {Ns} hands know a little more than they did this morning.
fails: The part is still wrong at closing time, and {N} goes home turning it over.
fails: {N} fixes one fault and finds two more behind it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- craft practice, high rungs (cycle 2)

== the season the hard jobs come to {N}
tier: life event
shape: craft
kind: practice
rungs: 2 3 4
fork:
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: work, interests
horizon: months
roles: colleague, mentor, rival, regular
earth: a season of steady work at {aim.place}, when people bring the hard jobs to {N}
tribal: a season when the clan brings its hardest work to {Ns} fire
magic: a season when the tower sends its hardest commissions to {Ns} bench
scene: These days the hard jobs come to {N}. There is a queue of them at {aim.place}, someone new is watching how {N} works, and there is less time than ever for the work {N} wants to try.
scene tribal: The clan brings its hardest work to {Ns} fire now, and a young one sits close to watch. There is little time left over for the thing {N} has wanted to try for years.
scene magic: The tower sends its hardest commissions to {Ns} bench, and an apprentice has been told to watch. The work {N} dreams of waits under a cloth in the corner.
- W | keep to the standard you are known for on every single job | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 82
- U | set aside one morning a week to try a new method | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | take only the jobs that carry your name further | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 66
- R | drop the queue for a week and make the piece dreamed of for years | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 60
- G | take the season more slowly and keep evenings for the people at home | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | set fair prices and a waiting list, and keep to both | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 75
- B>G | take on an apprentice and let them carry the plain jobs | v: power, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: person colleague | chance: 72
- G>U | teach the new one by working beside them, slowly, the old way | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson teaching shows the gaps | chance: 78
- U>R | turn down two safe jobs to make room for one strange one | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark turned down a chance | chance: 62
- R>W | take a month off, then come back to the queue with fresh eyes | v: hedonism, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means time+.05 | chance: 80
works: The queue goes down and the work stays good, and someone comes back just to say so.
works: {N} tries the new way on one job, and it is better, and nobody but {N} can tell why.
fails: The season runs away with {N}, and the good intentions go into a drawer.
fails: One job goes wrong in a small, public way, and it takes a month to stop thinking about it.

