# ---------------------------------------------------------------- craft mentor (cycle 1)

== the one who could teach {N} properly
tier: life event
shape: craft
kind: mentor
rungs: 0 1 2
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: learning, interests
horizon: months
roles: mentor, friend, parent
earth: {aim.person} with a lifetime in the work, who might take {N} on
tribal: an old maker of the clan who has never taken a pupil, and is watching {N}
magic: a master of the tower who takes one pupil in ten years, and has asked {Ns} name
scene: For a month {aim.person} has watched {N} at {aim.place}, and today says it out loud: {N} may come in early on Saturdays, if {N} means it. Offers like this do not come twice, and Saturdays are already full.
scene tribal: The oldest maker of the clan has never taken a pupil. This season the old one keeps finding work for {N} to fetch and carry, and watching how {N} does it.
scene magic: A master of the tower takes one pupil in ten years, and has asked {Ns} name twice this week. The other apprentices have noticed.
- W | come every Saturday, on time, and do what you are told | v: conformity, tradition | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 82
- U | come with a list of questions, and write down every answer | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | come, and make sure you are the best pupil they have ever had | v: achievement, power | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R | say yes, then argue with every method they show | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: try | foot: lesson arguing is a way of learning | chance: 55
- G | thank them, and say Saturdays belong to the family for now | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: ease | foot: mark turned down a chance | chance: 85
- W>U | ask to come once a month and work on what they set in between | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 78
- U>B | swap what you know of the newer tools for their old tricks | v: self-direction, power | aim: try | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- B>R | turn up with your best piece and ask what is wrong with it | v: power, stimulation | aim: try | foot: lesson hard words help most | chance: 62
- R>G | bring {friend} along, so the Saturdays feel like your own | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 72
- G>W | offer to sweep up and fetch things, and learn by being near | v: benevolence, tradition | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 80
works: The Saturdays add up: {N} learns more in a season than in the two years before.
works: {aim.person} says little, but one day lets {N} do the hard part alone, and only watches.
fails: The two of them rub each other the wrong way, and the Saturdays thin out.
fails: {aim.person} is too busy after all, and the offer quietly goes away.

