- B>G | win {rival} over, and work side by side instead | v: power, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 60
- G>U | keep your head down and learn from an older hand for a while | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: person mentor | chance: 78
- U>R | propose a friendly match: the same job, two ways, and others judge | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: try | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 60
- R>W | tell {rival} to their face what you think, then shake hands | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: try | foot: door made a friend | chance: 58
works: The rivalry pulls {N} up: {N} has never worked this well, and {rival} has noticed.
works: Next time the good job goes to {N}, and {rival} is the first to say well done.
fails: {rival} gets the next one too, and {N} cannot quite let it go.
fails: The rivalry turns sour, and the room at {aim.place} goes cold when they are both in it.

